-- Assertions written by the independent wave-2 reader for parts sgh and sgi (a fresh agent that wrote its answers from the text before it opened any encoding),
-- kept here where the encoding was changed to agree with them. Each carries the reader's scenario number and the answer the reader expected.

-- reader scenario #591, s 33(8) (text line 5710): a copy of the resolution "must not be lodged ... before the expiration of 21 days" is an "until" bar (Guide line 94 (d)); the resolution was passed on 1 March 2026, no application was made, and lodging on 23 March 2026, the first day not barred, is not barred: expected JUST FALSE.
-- arguments: the day the resolution was passed; an application to the Court has been made; the day the Court determined the application; the day the copy would be lodged
#ASSERT `s 33(8) lodging the copy of the resolution on the day is barred` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 23 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
